@meta
  project: htmFX
  title: Declarative 3D, WebGPU & Spatial Simulation Companion for htmxUI
  version: 1.2.0
  runtime: hmlr@1.2
  repo: github.com/hyperlibs/htmFX
  license: MIT
  architecture: Decoupled Spatial Companion Layer & SpatialEdgeDB
  bundle_footprint_gzipped: 33.99 KB

@type CameraMode = orbit* | first_person | third_person | cinematic | fly
@type EnvPreset = space* | outdoor | cyberpunk | underwater | dungeon | desert | arctic | laboratory
@type AtmosPreset = clear* | cloudy | rainy | stormy | foggy | windy | snowy | sandstorm | nebula
@type EmitterType = burn | flare | radiate | splash | splatter | explode | implode | splinter | zap | slime | wave | 240_fx_catalogue

@model EnvConfig
  preset: EnvPreset
  atmos: AtmosPreset
  camera: CameraMode
  fog_density: float
  wind_speed_ms: float
  altitude_m: float
  turbulence_curl: float

@model SpatialEntity
  id: string
  mesh_src: string
  xyz: [float, float, float]
  rotation: [float, float, float]
  scale: [float, float, float]
  material: string

# htmFX: Declarative 3D & Spatial Engine Specification (v1.2.0)
A lightweight (33.99 KB gzipped), declarative WebGL/WebGPU companion for htmxUI. 
Eliminates 400-line Three.js boilerplate in favor of declarative HTML components (<hx-viewport>, <hx-mesh>), 240+ spatial physics FX, and FlatBuffer SpatialEdgeDB storage for >100,000 entities.

## Core Directives & Macros | @model EnvConfig
| preset     | atmos       | camera       | fog_density | wind_speed_ms | altitude_m | turbulence_curl |
| $space     | $nebula     | $orbit       |        0.00 |          0.00 |  1000000.0 |            0.00 |
| $outdoor   | $foggy      | $first_person|        0.08 |         12.50 |      500.0 |            0.45 |
| $cyberpunk | $rainy      | $cinematic   |        0.04 |          8.00 |       50.0 |            0.20 |
| $desert    | $sandstorm  | $orbit       |        0.15 |         25.00 |     1200.0 |            0.80 |
| $dungeon   | $clear      | $first_person|        0.02 |          0.00 |     -200.0 |            0.05 |

## Spatial Physics & Mathematical Foundations

### 1. Volumetric Exponential Height Fog Field
Equation: ρ(y) = ρ₀ · e^(-(y - y₀) / H)
- In valleys (y = 500m), air is dense (ρ ≈ 0.85).
- On mountain peaks (y = 2000m), air clears (ρ ≈ 0.02), creating a volumetric sea of clouds below the camera.

### 2. Inverse-Square Distance Attenuation for Point/Volume Emitters
Equation: I(d) = I₀ / (1 + k₁·d + k₂·d²)
- Applied to $burn, $explode, $zap, spatial 3D audio, and heat haze vertex distortion.

### 3. Supersonic Ballistics & Altitude Drag Solver
Equation: F_drag = -0.5 · ρ(y) · C_d(Mach) · A · ||v|| · v
- Trajectory integrated via 4th-Order Runge-Kutta (RK4) accounting for crosswind shear and material ricochet matrices.

### 4. Curl-Noise Wind Turbulence & Fluid Swirl
Equation: v_wind(x,y,z) = ∇ × ψ(x,y,z)
- Divergence-free incompressible fluid turbulence vector field driving foliage swaying and missile smoke trails.

## SpatialEdgeDB FlatBuffer Spatial Store (>1,000 Entities)
When spatial entity counts exceed 1,000 items, DOM node creation is bypassed. Entities are ingested into `htmFX.SpatialEdgeDB` (TypedArray FlatBuffers), rendering directly via WebGPU instanced draws with $O(1)$ spatial spatial indexing.

## Declarative Web Component API

```html
<!-- Instant AAA 3D Scene in 3 Lines of HTML -->
<script src="/htmx.js"></script>
<script src="/htmx-bolt.js"></script>
<script src="/htmfx.js"></script>

<hx-viewport 3denv="$outdoor" 
             3datmos="$foggy(density: 0.06), $windy(15m/s)" 
             3dcamera="$orbit">
  <hx-mesh id="target-mesh" src="/models/drone.gltf" xyz="0, 10, -50"></hx-mesh>
  <hx-particle type="nebula" count="5000" color="#6366f1"></hx-particle>
  <hx-light type="sun" direction="[1, -2, 1]" intensity="1.5"></hx-light>
</hx-viewport>
```

## Flat .mx Spatial Coordinate Representation (Zero Div Soup)

```mx
@viewport 1920x1080

# 3D Scene Declarations
@3d[0, 0, 0]:           3D.Env(preset: "$space", atmos: "$nebula")
@3d[0, 5, -20]:         3D.Mesh("/models/satellite.gltf", spin: 0.01)
@3d[0, 5, -20]:         3D.Emitter(type: "$burn", intensity: 0.8)

# 2D Screen Anchors (HTMXUI HUD)
@pin[top-left]:         Panel.HUD("Satellite Telemetry", sub: "WebGPU Active")
@pin[bottom-bar]:       ActionBar(
                          Button("⚡ Pulse Thruster", action: $flare('#target'); $sound('ping')),
                          Button("🛑 Emergency Halt", action: $freeze(), color: "rose")
                        )
@pin[top-right]:        TelemetryBadge("120 FPS", color: "emerald", pulse: true)
```

## Autonomous Handoff Protocol & Diagnostic Bridge
- Standalone Library: `dist/htmfx.js` (33.99 KB gzipped)
- HTMXUI Bridge: Autonomous directive scanner (`hx-3d`, `3denv`, `3datmos`, `3dfx`, `<hx-viewport>`) delegates to `window.htmFX.mount(el)`
- Missing Companion Diagnostic: `@diag FX-0404: htmFX spatial companion required for 3D rendering.`
- Fallback Pipeline: Auto-detects WebGPU (`navigator.gpu`) with seamless WebGL2 fallback.
